sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant C as MFA-authenticated patient
  participant H as Express route/controller
  participant S as Booking service
  participant P as PostgreSQL transaction
  C->>H: POST /v1/consultations + Idempotency-Key + slotId
  H->>H: Shared ingress, live auth, patient RBAC, rate limit, Zod
  H->>S: Actor, validated input, key, request ID
  S->>P: Begin; revalidate/lock actor and session
  S->>P: Claim actor-scoped key; compare fingerprint
  alt Completed identical request
    P-->>S: Decrypt original status/body
    S->>P: Commit without another business event
  else New logical request
    S->>P: Shared doctor lock, check active account
    S->>P: Slot FOR UPDATE; recheck future/open/unoccupied
    alt Slot unavailable
      S->>P: Save conflict outcome; commit
      P-->>S: 409
    else Slot available
      S->>P: Insert consultation (partial unique occupancy index)
      S->>P: Append audit and unique pending outbox with traceparent
      S->>P: Encrypt/store original result; COMMIT
      P-->>S: 201 and booking DTO
    end
  end
  S-->>H: Original status/body
  H-->>C: Response (safe same-key retry after lost response)
  Note over S,P: Any unexpected persistence failure rolls back all four writes
  Note over S,P: No Redis or external network call inside transaction
  Note over C,P: Cancellation locks actor/key, doctor, slot, consultation; validates state and commits cancellation/audit/outbox/result together
  Note over C,P: Phase 4 worker leases committed events, records receipts and compensates internal payments; no provider notifications
  participant W as Restricted worker
  participant O as OTel collector
  W->>P: Lease committed job with SKIP LOCKED and fencing
  P-->>W: ID-only payload and traceparent
  W->>O: Consumer span, safe SQL spans and outcome metrics
  W->>P: Receipt + any internal compensation + audit + fenced ack
  Note over W,P: Fake refund adapter runs outside transactions; crash recovery uses stable idempotency key
